  "subject": "TASK-006 D20有界消息缓冲修复后的完整G1同范围复证；独立新预注册，原失败与通过run/ITER不变",
  "hypothesis": "At one fixed commit, the real OIS/OIC/oi binaries satisfy every P1 vector of B1-B4 on SQLite 3.54.1 and PostgreSQL 18.6 with zero zero-tolerance events, release resources within T_close+1s after each vector, and meet the P1 quality gates (unit coverage of the delivery unit >=95%, race detector, fuzzing, vet, staticcheck, govulncheck). Raw b4-resource-v2 records independently demonstrate complete role snapshots, a pre-cleanup fixed baseline, exact Linux FD equality, goroutines within baseline +/-10, and three consecutive empty-channel samples inside the original 2-second cleanup deadline.",
  "alternatives": [
    "the implementation passes only on one backend",
    "vectors pass only with relaxed timing, retries or hand-picked subsets",
    "resource counters drift because teardown depends on peer cooperation",
    "the loop depends on business-specific code or a modified binary per target",
    "missing/invalid diagnostics are mistaken for zero-resource success",
    "a post-failure baseline or lost control connection hides leaked descriptors",
    "a forged final resource summary hides missing, out-of-order or late snapshots"
  ],
  "disproof": "Any required vector failing or skipped on a required backend, any ZERO-TOLERANCE line, a resource check that does not settle, a coverage total below 95%, a race report, a fuzz failure, or a vet/staticcheck/govulncheck finding refutes the hypothesis for this commit. Missing or timed-out steps make the run inconclusive, never a pass. Missing required cleanup checks, malformed resource snapshots, role/profile mismatch, changing PID within a check, or a final claim not derivable from three consecutive in-deadline raw samples fails TV-B4-03 and the original resource criterion.",
  "limitations": [
    "Single machine loopback topology of B4 §4 (GitHub-hosted ubuntu-24.04 runner); not the 1C1G target environment (G5) and not WAN latency",
    "Test configuration of B4 §3 (shortened T_close, heartbeat, license and idle values); values are not SLOs or capacity commitments",
    "Observations O1-O4 are recorded without pass lines except zero-tolerance events (B4 §6); readiness is always unknown in P1 (no probes, G2)",
    "This rerun preserves the P1 scope; it does not independently establish G4 backup/restore/migration, HA (G6), or real consumer/provider compatibility (G7).",
    "Synthetic deterministic HTTP fixtures T1-T3; two OICs are logically separate accesses on one host, not host isolation"
  ],
